    "lawCode": "Amd §202, Work Comp L",
    "lawSection": "Workers' Compensation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3291A\n\nSPONSOR: SALAZAR\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the workers' compensation law, in relation to covered\nemployment as a domestic worker for temporary disability benefits\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 would make a technical amendment to Chapter 481 of 2010, the\nDomestic Workers Bill of Rights. It would amend section 202(2) of the\nWorkers Compensation Law to clarify that domestic workers who work at\nleast twenty hours per week and meet the duration of employment standard\nof four weeks are covered under the temporary disability benefits law.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date of the bill.\n\n \nAMENDED BILL:\n\nThe A-print of the bill changes the effective date from immediately upon\nenactment to the 1st of January in the year following enactment.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would implement the original intent in the Domestic Workers\nBill of Rights (Chapter 481 of 2010) in amending section 201 (5) of the\nWorkers Compensation Law, which deleted the clause that had excluded\ndomestic workers who work less than 40 hours per week. The intent was to\nensure that domestic workers who work at least 20 hours per week (and\nmeet other requirements) are eligible for disability insurance. The\nSponsor's Memorandum on the Domestic Workers Bill of Rights stated, \"In\naddition, the bill grants disability insurance to part time domestic\nworkers...\". Unfortunately, the Domestic Workers Bill of Rights failed\nmake the necessary corresponding amendment to Workers Compensation Law\nsection 202 (2). In an August 31, 2010 letter to Governor Paterson, the\nWorkers Compensation Board stated its support of this proposal and urged\nthat this technical correction be made. This bill does so.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: A.1326/S.3961 - Passed Assembly 2/25/20\n\n2018: A.5758/ No Same as - Ordered to Third Reading\n\n2017: A.5758/ No Same as - Advanced to Third Reading\n\n2016: A.3504/S.2837 - Ordered to Third Reading in Assembly\n\n2014: A.6358/S.4234 - Passed Assembly, Advanced to Third Reading in\nSenate\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to New York State and its subdivisions.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on January 1st in the year following enact-\nment.\n",
